## Lobby

::bg{location="lobby" time="night"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Terrazzo floor, a map of the ward under cracked perspex, a wheelchair facing the wall like a child in disgrace.
@narrator{code="0020"}: On the reception counter by the door, somebody has left a paraffin lantern. The glass is still warm.
@nell{code="0010" mono}: Toby's. He always overpacks.
@narrator{code="0030"}: A brass plaque by the stairs catches the lantern's reflection.
@narrator{code="0040"}: Corridors run off in every direction: reception, the chapel, the children's ward, the hydrotherapy suite. Signs for the pharmacy, the records room and the morgue point down corridors with their doors shut.
